    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qyh97z1",
      "content": "BALCO is located at Korba, Chhattisgarh. It was set up as a public sector enterprise in 1965. Vedanta Ltd. (formerly Sterlite Industries) acquired a 51% stake in BALCO in 2001 through strategic disinvestment by the Government of India. BALCO uses bauxite deposits from Chhattisgarh and neighboring Odisha for aluminium production."
    },
    {
      "id": "ype2k4k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.3 SECL (South Eastern Coalfields Limited)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vlrrg0t",
      "content": "SECL is a subsidiary of Coal India Limited (CIL) and is headquartered in Bilaspur, Chhattisgarh. It operates in Chhattisgarh and Madhya Pradesh. The coalfields of Korba (Korea, Raigarh) are among the most productive in the country. SECL is one of the largest coal producers in India."
    },
